<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jamgön Kongtrul</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1813–1899</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Jamgön Kongtrul Lodrö Thayé</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jamgön Kongtrul Lodrö Thayé was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibetan-buddhism">Tibetan Buddhist</a> scholar and teacher from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kham">Kham</a> and one of the founders of the non-sectarian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rime-movement">Rimé movement</a>. Working with Jamyang Khyentse Wangpo, he gathered teachings from all the Tibetan traditions into vast collections known as the Five Treasuries. He was based at Palpung Monastery in the kingdom of Derge.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jamgon-kongtrul.jpg" alt="Jamgön Kongtrul" width="240" height="316" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lodro_Thaye.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
